{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-point","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:categorical-point","kind":"definition","title":"Categorical point","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-universe"],"tags":["point","categorical"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalPoint","text":"categorical-point.md","leanSource":"categorical-point.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:categorical-point\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum universe. A <strong>categorical point</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is a morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code>. The augmentation ideal at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}_p = \\ker(p^* \\colon A \\to \\mathbf{1})</code>, and the germ of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> is the quotient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A / \\mathfrak{m}_p^2</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-point.md","heading":"Definition","number":"4.16.7","page":"b/def-categorical-point","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":67},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalPoint","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-point.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
